// `json.parse::<T>` is rejected at check time when `T` has no JSON decoding — an enum here (a sum
// with no canonical JSON form; only value structs, scalars, lists, options and string-keyed maps
// decode). A compile-time E0007, so both backends agree (the program never runs).
// expect: error E0007 at 7:5
use std.{json};
enum Color { Red; Green; Blue; }
c = json.parse::<Color>("\"Red\"");
echo c;
